      "title": "MOC H3 authoring/preflight example",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Authoring and preflight only\nThis graph intentionally uses two generated placeholder images, so it can queue without H3 checkpoints or uploaded media. Replace each **Empty Image** node with a real image loader when authoring a shot. Connect a loader's **MASK** output to the matching Image Reference when source isolation is needed; the report shows retained coverage and bounds. Masks isolate source evidence and do not control output placement.\n\nThe Compile node is an output node and displays its mapping and diagnostics inline. It does **not** encode or sample video. For full generation, open ComfyUI's official MiniMax H3 R2V template and replace its native reference-authoring node with the MOC builders, Reference Set, and Reference to Video+. Keep signal weights at `1.0` unless the experimental MODEL patch is visibly connected to the sampling path."
      ]
    }
